## Design Principles

### Do

- Create clean, modern, and visually appealing interfaces.
- Maintain consistent spacing throughout the application.
- Follow a consistent typography hierarchy.
- Keep layouts simple and uncluttered.
- Maintain consistent border radius, shadows, and colors.
- Align elements properly.
- Use whitespace to improve readability.
- Build reusable UI components.
- Follow the existing design system.
- Design with scalability in mind.

### Don't

- Don't create inconsistent layouts.
- Don't use random spacing values.
- Don't mix multiple design styles.
- Don't overuse colors.
- Don't overuse gradients.
- Don't overuse shadows.
- Don't create visually noisy interfaces.
- Don't sacrifice usability for aesthetics.

---

## Layout Standards

Always create layouts that include:

- Clear page heading
- Page description when needed
- Well-structured content sections
- Consistent spacing
- Proper alignment
- Responsive containers
- Sticky actions where appropriate

Maintain proper spacing between:

- Sections
- Cards
- Inputs
- Buttons
- Tables
- Dialogs

---

## Responsive Design

Every page must work perfectly on:

- Mobile
- Tablet
- Laptop
- Desktop
- Large screens

Always:

- Use responsive Tailwind classes.
- Prefer Flexbox and Grid.
- Avoid fixed widths.
- Use responsive typography.
- Test layouts for small screens.

Never allow:

- Horizontal scrolling
- Overflowing content
- Broken layouts
- Hidden buttons

---

## User Experience

Every screen should provide:

- Loading State
- Empty State
- Error State
- Success State
- Disabled State

Always inform users what is happening.

Never leave users waiting without feedback.

Examples:

- Skeleton loaders
- Loading spinners
- Empty illustrations
- Helpful error messages
- Success toasts
- Confirmation dialogs

---

## Forms

Forms should always:

- Show labels.
- Show helper text when needed.
- Validate inputs.
- Display inline validation errors.
- Focus the first invalid field.
- Preserve user input.
- Disable submit while loading.
- Prevent duplicate submissions.
- Show success/error feedback.

Use:

- React Hook Form
- Zod
- Toast notifications

---

## Tables

Tables should support when applicable:

- Search
- Sorting
- Filtering
- Pagination
- Bulk actions
- Export
- Row selection

Always provide:

- Loading skeleton
- Empty state
- Error state

---

## Cards

Cards should:

- Have consistent padding.
- Have subtle shadows.
- Use rounded corners.
- Maintain consistent spacing.
- Include hover feedback when clickable.

Avoid overcrowding cards.

---

## Buttons

Buttons should always have:

- Hover state
- Active state
- Disabled state
- Loading state
- Focus state

Primary actions should be visually prominent.

Danger actions should require confirmation.

---

## Dialogs

Dialogs should:

- Open smoothly.
- Close smoothly.
- Trap keyboard focus.
- Support Escape key.
- Close when appropriate.
- Prevent accidental destructive actions.

---

## Navigation

Navigation should:

- Clearly indicate active routes.
- Support keyboard navigation.
- Use breadcrumbs where appropriate.
- Highlight current page.
- Be intuitive and predictable.

---

## Animations

Animations should improve user experience—not distract from it.

Use animations for:

- Page transitions
- Card appearance
- Modal open/close
- Drawer transitions
- Sidebar collapse
- Dropdown menus
- Accordions
- Toast notifications
- Hover interactions
- Loading transitions
- Skeleton loading
- List animations

Preferred libraries:

- Framer Motion
- Tailwind transitions
- CSS transforms

Animation duration:

150–300ms

Use:

- ease-in-out
- ease-out

Avoid:

- Long animations
- Excessive movement
- Bouncing everywhere
- Flashing effects
- Distracting transitions

Respect:

prefers-reduced-motion

---

## Icons

Use icons only when they improve usability.

Prefer:

- lucide-react

Keep icon sizes consistent.

Don't mix multiple icon libraries.

---

## Colors

Use colors consistently.

Primary colors:

- Main actions

Secondary colors:

- Supporting actions

Success:

- Completed actions

Warning:

- Caution

Danger:

- Delete
- Errors

Never rely only on color to communicate information.

---

## Accessibility

Always:

- Use semantic HTML.
- Use accessible labels.
- Add aria attributes.
- Support keyboard navigation.
- Maintain proper color contrast.
- Show visible focus indicators.
- Add alt text to images.
- Use descriptive button labels.

Never:

- Hide focus outlines.
- Use inaccessible color combinations.

---

## Performance

Optimize UI by:

- Lazy loading heavy components.
- Code splitting pages.
- Memoizing expensive calculations.
- Preventing unnecessary re-renders.
- Optimizing images.
- Virtualizing very large lists.

Don't optimize prematurely.

---

## Empty States

Every empty state should include:

- Meaningful illustration or icon
- Clear title
- Helpful description
- Primary action when applicable

Never display blank screens.

---

## Error Handling

Always show user-friendly errors.

Include:

- Clear explanation
- Recovery action
- Retry button when possible

Never expose raw API errors directly to users.

---

## Loading States

Always provide:

- Skeleton loaders
- Progress indicators
- Loading buttons
- Page loading states

Never allow layout shifts while loading.

---

## Dashboard Standards

Dashboard pages should include:

- Summary cards
- Search
- Filters
- Tables
- Pagination
- Export
- Bulk actions
- Responsive charts
- Proper loading states

Maintain consistent dashboard spacing.

---

## Final UI Review Checklist

Before considering UI complete, verify:

✓ Modern and visually appealing

✓ Responsive on all devices

✓ Consistent spacing

✓ Proper typography

✓ Accessible

✓ Smooth animations

✓ Loading states implemented

✓ Empty states implemented

✓ Error states implemented

✓ Success feedback implemented

✓ Forms properly validated

✓ Tables are user-friendly

✓ Buttons have proper states

✓ No layout shifts

✓ No overflowing content

✓ Performance optimized

✓ Follows existing design system

✓ Production-ready appearance
